From: ReForge <reforge@localhost>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] update_manager: allow zip updates for reserved klipper/moonraker

Moonraker handles the "klipper" and "moonraker" updaters specially: their
config is built from a hardcoded BASE_CONFIG plus only OPTION_OVERRIDES
("channel", "pinned_commit", "refresh_interval", "report_anomalies"), and
their `type` comes from AppType.detect() (NOT from the section's `type`
option). Upstream detect() returns only GIT_REPO / PYTHON / NONE, so a
zip-deployed klipper/moonraker is typed NONE and cannot be updated via
update_manager. Any type/repo/path/managed_services set in those sections is
silently dropped, producing "Unparsed config option" warnings.

ReForge ships klipper and moonraker as prebuilt zip releases (the gcc-less
device never recompiles), so they must be ZIP-type updaters like our other
components. Three minimal changes:

  1. detect(): a directory carrying release_info.json (how a zip deploy marks
     itself - see net_deploy.py) is detected as ZIP. Git detection still wins;
     the moonraker self path falls back to source_info.source_path().
  2. OPTION_OVERRIDES: add "repo" so the reserved updaters read their repo from
     the section (NetDeploy requires it; BASE_CONFIG has none). path is derived
     (klippy connection / source_path) and managed_services defaults to the
     updater name, so neither needs to be configured.
  3. _configure_virtualenv(): skip the env->virtualenv derivation for ZIP
     deploys. When the klipper updater is rebuilt on server:klippy_identified it
     carries an 'env' (klippy's python_path, e.g. /usr/bin/python3, or the
     default ~/klippy-env). A ZIP klipper is prebuilt on the system python with
     a bundled c_helper.so - there is no virtualenv. Without this guard NetDeploy
     derives a venv as python.parent.parent (e.g. /usr), finds no bin/activate,
     and aborts the whole klipper updater ("Invalid virtualenv at path /usr").
     Guarding the ZIP case makes klipper behave like any other zip updater.

Signed-off-by: ReForge <reforge@localhost>
--- a/moonraker/components/update_manager/common.py
+++ b/moonraker/components/update_manager/common.py
@@ -42,7 +42,9 @@
     }
 }
 
-OPTION_OVERRIDES = ("channel", "pinned_commit", "refresh_interval", "report_anomalies")
+OPTION_OVERRIDES = (
+    "channel", "pinned_commit", "refresh_interval", "report_anomalies", "repo"
+)
 
 class AppType(ExtendedEnum):
     NONE = 1
@@ -59,10 +61,16 @@
             app_path = pathlib.Path(app_path).expanduser()
         if source_info.is_git_repo(app_path):
             return AppType.GIT_REPO
-        elif app_path is None and source_info.is_vitualenv_project():
+        # ReForge: a directory carrying release_info.json is a zip-deployed app.
+        # Upstream detect() yields only GIT_REPO/PYTHON/NONE, so the reserved
+        # 'klipper'/'moonraker' updaters (type comes from detect(), not config)
+        # could never be ZIP. Detect it so they can be OTA-updated like the rest.
+        ri_dir = app_path if app_path is not None else source_info.source_path()
+        if ri_dir is not None and (ri_dir / "release_info.json").exists():
+            return AppType.ZIP
+        if app_path is None and source_info.is_vitualenv_project():
             return AppType.PYTHON
-        else:
-            return AppType.NONE
+        return AppType.NONE
 
     @classmethod
     def valid_types(cls) -> List[AppType]:
--- a/moonraker/components/update_manager/app_deploy.py
+++ b/moonraker/components/update_manager/app_deploy.py
@@ -89,7 +89,12 @@
             if not venv_path.is_absolute():
                 venv_path = self.path.joinpath(venv_path)
             self._verify_path(config, 'virtualenv', venv_path, check_file=False)
-        elif config.has_option("env"):
+        elif config.has_option("env") and self.type != AppType.ZIP:
+            # ReForge: skip the env->virtualenv derivation for ZIP deploys. A
+            # zip-deployed app (e.g. our reserved klipper) is prebuilt and runs
+            # on the system python with no virtualenv; get_base_configuration
+            # still injects a default/system 'env', and without this guard
+            # NetDeploy would build a bogus venv from it and abort the updater.
             # Deprecated
             if self.name != "klipper":
                 self.log_info("Option 'env' is deprecated, use 'virtualenv' instead.")
@@ -124,6 +129,12 @@
     def _configure_dependencies(
         self, config: ConfigHelper, node_only: bool = False
     ) -> None:
+        if self.type == AppType.ZIP:
+            # ReForge: a ZIP deploy is prebuilt - no pip requirements, system
+            # dependencies, or install script to verify. Those are git/source
+            # install concepts that BASE_CONFIG injects for the reserved
+            # klipper/moonraker updaters and would otherwise abort the updater.
+            return
         if config.getboolean("enable_node_updates", False):
             self.npm_pkg_json = self.path.joinpath("package-lock.json")
             self._verify_path(config, 'enable_node_updates', self.npm_pkg_json)
